# Summary (generated by summarize_cell.py; nothing edited by hand)

## Gate
selection: interpretable (variant as_written)

| item | core | passed | detail |
|---|---|---|---|
| G9 x | True | True |  |
| G1 x | True | True |  |
| G7 x | True | True |  |
| G8 x | True | True |  |
| [as_written] G4 | True | True |  |
| [as_written] G5 | True | True |  |

## Primary: true template, 900 ms window (variant as_written)

- LIP: under the block permutation test, which assumes that blocks are exchangeable under the null, with the colour-selection penalty unmodelled, template decoding is not established (Holm-adjusted p = 0.7500). With 3 to 4 blocks per bin the test has limited power and this result does not show that the template is absent.
- FEF: under the block permutation test, which assumes that blocks are exchangeable under the null, with the colour-selection penalty unmodelled, template decoding is not established (Holm-adjusted p = 0.7500). With 3 to 4 blocks per bin the test has limited power and this result does not show that the template is absent.
- LPFC: under the block permutation test, which assumes that blocks are exchangeable under the null, with the colour-selection penalty unmodelled, template decoding is not established (Holm-adjusted p = 0.7500). With 3 to 4 blocks per bin the test has limited power and this result does not show that the template is absent.

## Design counts and the chosen C at the upper edge (log10 C = 1)

- primary: observed N_progression 69, N_neurons 25; 2 of 3 permutations differ from the observed design or are undefined (0 undefined)
- primary: share of SVM fits with chosen C at the upper edge: {'LIP': 0.167, 'FEF': 0.0, 'LPFC': 0.0}

